# Feed media

Only the in-view ("focused") feed cell mounts a real `expo-video` player. Every other
video cell renders the lightweight `FeedVideoPoster` (play button), or feeds show
blank/black tiles while many off-screen players initialize.

- In `PostMediaBlock`, `feedMediaFocused === false` means "feed cell, not focused" →
  render the poster, not `CapsuleVideoPlayer`. `undefined` means detail screen → real
  player. Don't collapse these three states.

# Feed images (no blank tiles)

Posts whose image shows only after you tap into the detail screen = the feed list
clipped/cancelled the load and never repainted.

- The home feed `FlatList` MUST keep `removeClippedSubviews={false}`. Clipping detaches
  cells the list thinks are off-screen and frequently fails to re-attach their media.
  Memory stays bounded via `windowSize` (and `maxToRenderPerBatch`), not clipping.
- Because clipping is off (it also broke `onEndReached` scroll measurement), load-more
  MUST run from the proximity-scroll fallback in `handleScroll` on **all** platforms,
  not just iOS. `handleLoadMore` is `loadingMoreRef`-guarded so it can't double-fetch.
- `PostMediaBlock` images must self-heal: `onError` remounts the `<Image/>` (bump a
  reload key) up to a small cap so a cancelled/transient load isn't stuck blank.

# Library caching (no "rolling" loader)

Navigating into a category must NOT show a full-screen spinner when data is pre-warmed.

- Read the cache first with `peekLibraryCache` and render immediately
  (stale-while-revalidate); only `setLoading(true)` when there is no cached data.
- When pre-warming from the library grid, call `fetchLibraryCached(url, token)` WITHOUT
  `{ force: true }` so the in-flight request is shared (de-duped) with the category
  screen's fetch instead of firing a duplicate.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — duplicate network request, defeats de-dupe
void fetchLibraryCached(url, token, { force: true });

// ✅ GOOD
void fetchLibraryCached(url, token);
```
